# Moodle Hooks API + AMD (Marketplace compliance)

ArtQTM Light targets **Moodle 4.5+**. Follow core conventions so HQ / moodle.org CI passes.

## Hooks API — not magic lib.php callbacks

Moodle 4.4+ deprecates `<plugin>_extend_navigation`, `<plugin>_before_http_headers`, etc.

| Legacy (do not add) | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `local_artqtml_extend_navigation()` in `lib.php` | `\core\hook\navigation\primary_extend` listener in `classes/hook_callbacks.php`, registered in `db/hooks.php` |
| Other magic callbacks | Matching class under `lib/classes/hook/` in core — register in `db/hooks.php` |

**Pattern:**

```php
// db/hooks.php
[
    'hook' => \core\hook\navigation\primary_extend::class,
    'callback' => [\local_artqtml\hook_callbacks::class, 'extend_primary_navigation'],
],

// classes/hook_callbacks.php
public static function extend_primary_navigation(primary_extend $hook): void {
    $hook->get_primaryview()->add_node($node);
}
```

After changing `db/hooks.php`: purge caches (`php admin/cli/purge_caches.php`).

## AMD JavaScript — not `$PAGE->requires->js()`

**Never** load plugin JS from a top-level `js/` folder:

```php
// BAD — legacy, fails C-12 / HQ review
$PAGE->requires->js(new moodle_url('/local/artqtml/js/foo.js'));
echo html_writer::script('window.MyGlobal.init(...)');
```

**Required pattern:**

1. Source in `amd/src/<module>.js` (use `define([...], function(...) {` like existing `uploadconflict.js`, or ES6 `export` if the plugin already uses it consistently).
2. Build: `cd /path/to/moodle && npx grunt amd --root=local/artqtml`
3. Commit `amd/build/*.min.js` (+ `.map` if generated).
4. Load from PHP: `$PAGE->requires->js_call_amd('local_artqtml/<module>', 'init', [$args]);`
5. Prefer `core/ajax`, `core/str`, `core/notification` over raw `fetch` / `M.cfg` globals.

**Why:** Moodle's JS pipeline (RequireJS, caching, minification, PHPUnit AMD tests) expects AMD. Plain `js/` files bypass that and trigger compliance findings (C-12).

## Checklist for new UI behaviour

- [ ] Hook listener in `hook_callbacks` + `db/hooks.php` (not `lib.php` magic name)
- [ ] AMD module in `amd/src/`, not `js/`
- [ ] `grunt amd` run; build artefacts committed
- [ ] PHP loads via `js_call_amd` only; no inline `<script>` init blocks
- [ ] Lang strings passed as `js_call_amd` arguments (or `get_string` in templates), not hardcoded in JS
